      <h2 id="bio-heading">Education, Teaching &amp; Training</h2>
      <span class="gold-rule"></span>
      <p>Dr. John Pasicznyk earned his Doctor of Dental Surgery degree from Indiana University School of Dentistry. He has built his career around implant surgery and full-arch reconstruction — the cases where planning, surgery, and the final teeth all have to come together.</p>
      <p>He has served as faculty and mentor with 3D Dentists and Implant Pathway, where he teaches implant surgery to practicing dentists. He is a clinical advisor to Dentsply Sirona on same-day chairside CAD/CAM and 3D cone-beam imaging, and took part in the clinical validation of CEREC Tessera, a same-day ceramic restoration material.</p>
      <p>At Foundation, he does not hand cases off. The doctor who plans your treatment is the doctor who performs your surgery and restores your final teeth.</p>

